TASK FIX45
	TITLE "validation refuses a save whose section 0 carries no entry, before any merge and any"
		+ "write"
	STATUS implemented
	DELIVERED_BY 102
	SPEC "Validation returns an issue for a save whose section 0 carries no entry, and the merge is"
		+ "not attempted"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/validateSaveContent.spec.js"
	SPEC "mergeGlobalMetadata called with two empty sections fails with a named error, never with a"
		+ "bare TypeError, and the spec covers this case"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/mergeGlobalMetadata.spec.ts"
	SPEC "bun merge on a folder of two saves with an empty section 0 shows the validation refusal"
		+ "in business language and writes no file"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/initMergeCli.spec.js"
	AFTER @TASK.TEST44
	RATIONALE "The fix is a follow-up ruled by the user on 2026-09-16: pull request #15 does not"
		+ "change the merge behaviour on this case, it replaces a corrupted save written silently"
		+ "by a loud failure with no write. The path the error takes is already settled: an error"
		+ "on an input file belongs to validation, the same error reached further is a broken"
		+ "invariant that fails loudly. The case is reachable end to end: splitSectionLines returns"
		+ "an empty array for an empty section, verifySectionCount only counts the parts, and"
		+ "validateSchemas loops over the entries of a section so finds nothing wrong with zero"
		+ "entries; the minItems that would forbid it lives in save-file.schema.json, which no code"
		+ "compiles, only the ten per-entry schemas being compiled. The layer of the error type is"
		+ "left to the task: the named error directory covers only the core-mapping infrastructure,"
		+ "and mergeGlobalMetadata is a domain rule"
		REF @DECISION.AnEmptyMetadataSectionIsRefusedByValidation
		REF @DECISION.AnErrorsOriginDecidesItsPath
		REF @DECISION.ABrokenInvariantFailsWithANamedErrorType
	SOURCE "Review of pull request #15 and user ruling of 2026-09-16"
		PR 15

